Provenance of the colour values in this package
================================================

Only colour values are taken from the sources below: no code, no theme files.

1. Doom Emacs themes
--------------------

data/doom.json holds colours of the Doom Emacs themes, from
https://github.com/doomemacs/themes on its main branch, commit
a59202912ad55014e53a685eee6cd94130bdd4fd (2026-08-26). For each chosen theme it
holds the GUI value of bg, bg-alt, base0 to base8, fg, fg-alt, the named colours
(red, orange, green, teal, yellow, blue, dark-blue, magenta, violet, cyan,
dark-cyan) and the syntax classes (comments, strings, keywords, numbers,
constants, variables, functions, type, operators). scripts/extract-doom.mjs read
them as text from themes/doom-<theme>-theme.el:

  node scripts/extract-doom.mjs <clone>/themes <commit>

The themes are those of two lists in data/doom.json: «paletas», the Doom
palettes, and «soloEnfasis», the hand-written palettes that take only their
emphasis swatches from Doom (since 2026-11-16: gruvbox, from doom-gruvbox and
doom-gruvbox-light; monokai, from doom-monokai-classic). They were extracted from
the same commit.

On 2026-11-16 the reader learnt one more form, for doom-gruvbox's and
doom-gruvbox-light's bg and bg-alt: (cond ((equal option "value") x) … (t y)),
resolved, like if, with the default value of the option's defcustom (nil, t or a
string); any other form of cond is an error. With their defcustoms at nil, the
final t applies: the default variant, neither hard nor soft, which is our
gruvbox's (bg #282828 and #fbf1c7).

The data are not edited by hand: for another commit or theme, change the
«paletas» (or «soloEnfasis») list in data/doom.json, extract again with the new
commit (and update this file) and regenerate the palettes with `npm run doom`.

The city-lights palette was not imported: its upstream states CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
(see the table below), so its theme was removed from data/doom.json.

