2. The upstream schemes the Doom themes port
---------------------------------------------

Each Doom theme ports an upstream colour scheme, or is original to Doom. The
licence is the one the upstream itself states; "unconfirmed" means it could not
be confirmed from the upstream (checked 2026-11-19).

  palette          upstream                                              licence
  acario           Doom original                                         (Doom, MIT)
  ayu              https://github.com/dempfi/ayu                         MIT
  bluloco          https://github.com/uloco/theme-bluloco-dark (-light)  LGPL-3.0
  challenger-deep  https://github.com/challenger-deep-theme/vim          MIT
  dark-plus        VS Code's Dark+ (Doom names no source URL)            unconfirmed
  dracula          https://github.com/dracula/dracula-theme              MIT
  earl-grey        Doom original                                         (Doom, MIT)
  flatwhite        https://github.com/biletskyy/flatwhite-syntax         MIT
  henna            https://github.com/httpsterio/vscode-henna            unconfirmed
  horizon          https://github.com/jolaleye/horizon-theme-vscode      MIT
  material         https://github.com/material-theme/vsc-material-theme  unconfirmed
  nord             https://github.com/nordtheme/nord                     MIT
  nova             https://github.com/trevordmiller/nova-colors          unconfirmed
                   (npm metadata says MIT; no licence file seen)
  oceanic-next     https://github.com/voronianski/oceanic-next-color-scheme  MIT
  one              https://github.com/atom/one-dark-ui (and one-light-ui)    MIT
  peacock          https://github.com/daylerees/colour-schemes           MIT
  rouge            https://github.com/josefaidt/rouge-theme              MIT
  solarized        https://github.com/altercation/solarized              MIT
  sourcerer        https://github.com/xero/sourcerer                     unconfirmed
                   (states "free", no SPDX licence)
  spacegrey        https://github.com/SublimeText/Spacegray              MIT
  tokyo-night      https://github.com/tokyo-night/tokyo-night-vscode-theme  MIT
  tomorrow         https://github.com/chriskempson/tomorrow-theme        MIT
  vibrant          Doom original (a variant of doom-one; see one)        (Doom, MIT)
  xcode            Apple's Xcode default theme (no upstream repository)  unconfirmed
  zenburn          https://github.com/bbatsov/zenburn-emacs (Emacs port) GPL-3.0
  city-lights      https://github.com/Yummygum/city-lights-syntax-vsc    CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
                   (NOT imported)

3. The hand-written palettes
----------------------------

  gruvbox  https://github.com/morhetz/gruvbox, MIT (stated in its README and
           package.json). Its values are also the chord graph's "gruvbox" theme
           (graph src/themes.ts).
  monokai  The base16 Monokai scheme (author stated as Wimer Hazenberg),
           https://github.com/tinted-theming/schemes (base16/monokai.yaml), MIT.
  neutra   The owner's own values. Its code colours (#116329, #0550ae; #7ee787,
           #79c0ff, #ff7b72, #d2a8ff, #ffa657) are GitHub Primer palette values
           (https://github.com/primer/primitives, MIT); the remaining code hues'
           origin is unconfirmed. Its graph roles are derived from its own roles
           by scripts/doom.mjs's graph rules.
